nType: string;\n  userId: string;\n  username: string;\n  targetType: string;\n  targetId: string;\n  targetName: string;\n  details?: Record<string, unknown>;\n  timestamp: Date;\n}\n\nexport interface AuthRequest extends Request {\n  user?: User;\n}\n```\n\nWait, for AuthRequest I need to import Request from express. Let me handle that.\n\nNow `src/store.ts`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { randomUUID } from 'crypto';\nimport { User, Folder, Document, ShareEntry, ActivityEntry, Role, ResourceType } from './types.js';\n\nclass Store {\n  users: Map<string, User> = new Map();\n  usersByUsername: Map<string, User> = new Map();\n  folders: Map<string, Folder> = new Map();\n  documents: Map<string, Document> = new Map();\n  shares: ShareEntry[] = [];\n  activities: ActivityEntry[] = [];\n  tokens: Map<string, string> = new Map(); // token -> userId\n\n  // User methods\n  createUser(username: string, passwordHash: string): User {\n    const id = randomUUID();\n    const user: User = { id, username, passwordHash, createdAt: new Date() };\n    this.users.set(id, user);\n    this.usersByUsername.set(username, user);\n    return user;\n  }\n\n  getUserById(id: string): User | undefined {\n    return this.users.get(id);\n  }\n\n  getUserByUsername(username: string): User | undefined {\n    return this.usersByUsername.get(username);\n  }\n\n  // Token methods\n  createToken(userId: string): string {\n    const token = randomUUID();\n    this.tokens.set(token, userId);\n    return token;\n  }\n\n  getUserIdByToken(token: string): string | undefined {\n    return this.tokens.get(token);\n  }\n\n  // Folder methods\n  createFolder(name: string, parentId: string | null, ownerId: string): Folder {\n    const id = randomUUID();\n    const folder: Folder = { id, name, parentId, ownerId, createdAt: new Date(), updatedAt: new Date() };\n    this.folders.set(id, folder);\n    return folder;\n  }\n\n  getFolder(id: string): Folder | undefined {\n    return this.folders.get(id);\n  }\n\n  updateFolder(id: string, name: string): Folder | undefined {\n    const folder = this.folders.get(id);\n    if (!folder) return undefined;\n    folder.name = name;\n    folder.updatedAt = new Date();\n    return folder;\n  }\n\n  deleteFolder(id: string): void {\n    // Delete all child folders recursively\n    const childFolders = Array.from(this.folders.values()).filter(f => f.parentId === id);\n    for (const child of childFolders) {\n      this.deleteFolder(child.id);\n    }\n    \n    // Delete all documents in this folder\n    const docsInFolder = Array.from(this.documents.values()).filter(d => d.folderId === id);\n    for (const doc of docsInFolder) {\n      this.deleteDocument(doc.id);\n    }\n    \n    // Delete share entries for this folder\n    this.shares = this.shares.filter(s => !(s.resourceType === 'folder' && s.resourceId === id));\n    \n    // Remove the folder\n    this.folders.delete(id);\n  }\n\n  getChildFolders(parentId: string): Folder[] {\n    return Array.from(this.folders.values()).filter(f => f.parentId === parentId);\n  }\n\n  // Document methods\n  createDocument(title: string, content: string, folderId: string, ownerId: string): Document {\n    const id = randomUUID();\n    const doc: Document = { id, title, content, folderId, ownerId, createdAt: new Date(), updatedAt: new Date() };\n    this.documents.set(id, doc);\n    return doc;\n  }\n\n  getDocument(id: string): Document | undefined {\n    return this.documents.get(id);\n  }\n\n  updateDocument(id: string, title: string, content: string): Document | undefined {\n    const doc = this.documents.get(id);\n    if (!doc) return undefined;\n    doc.title = title;\n    doc.content = content;\n    doc.updatedAt = new Date();\n    return doc;\n  }\n\n  deleteDocument(id: string): void {\n    // Delete share entries for this document\n    this.shares = this.shares.filter(s => !(s.resourceType === 'document' && s.resourceId === id));\n    this.documents.delete(id);\n  }\n\n  getDocumentsInFolder(folderId: string): Document[] {\n    return Array.from(this.documents.values()).filter(d => d.folderId === folderId);\n  }\n\n  // Share methods\n  shareResource(resourceType: ResourceType, resourceId: string, userId: string, role: Role, sharedBy: string): ShareEntry {\n    // Remove existing share if any\n    this.shares = this.shares.filter(s => !(s.resourceType === resourceType && s.resourceId === resourceId && s.userId === userId));\n    \n    const entry: ShareEntry = {\n      id: randomUUID(),\n      resourceType,\n      resourceId,\n      userId,\n      role,\n      sharedBy,\n      createdAt: new Date(),\n    };\n    this.shares.push(entry);\n    return entry;\n  }\n\n  getSharesForResource(resourceType: ResourceType, resourceId: string): ShareEntry[] {\n    return this.shares.filter(s => s.resourceType === resourceType && s.resourceId === resourceId);\n  }\n\n  // Effective permission calculation\n  private roleValue(role: Role | null): number {\n    if (!role) return 0;\n    return { viewer: 1, editor: 2, owner: 3 }[role];\n  }\n\n  private roleFromValue(value: number): Role | null {\n    if (value <= 0) return null;\n    if (value === 1) return 'viewer';\n    if (value === 2) return 'editor';\n    return 'owner';\n  }\n\n  getEffectiveFolderPermission(folderId: string, userId: string): Role | null {\n    const folder = this.folders.get(folderId);\n    if (!folder) return null;\n    \n    // Owner always has owner access\n    if (folder.ownerId === userId) return 'owner';\n    \n    let maxRole = 0;\n    \n    // Walk up the folder tree\n    let currentId: string | null = folderId;\n    while (currentId) {\n      const currentFolder = this.folders.get(currentId);\n      if (!currentFolder) break;\n      \n      // Check direct shares on this folder\n      const share = this.shares.find(s => s.resourceType === 'folder' && s.resourceId === currentId && s.userId === userId);\n      if (share) {\n        maxRole = Math.max(maxRole, this.roleValue(share.role));\n      }\n      \n      currentId = currentFolder.parentId;\n    }\n    \n    return this.roleFromValue(maxRole);\n  }\n\n  getEffectiveDocumentPermission(docId: string, userId: string): Role | null {\n    const doc = this.documents.get(docId);\n    if (!doc) return null;\n    \n    // Owner always has owner access\n    if (doc.ownerId === userId) return 'owner';\n    \n    let maxRole = 0;\n    \n    // Check direct share on document\n    const directShare = this.shares.find(s => s.resourceType === 'document' && s.resourceId === docId && s.userId === userId);\n    if (directShare) {\n      maxRole = Math.max(maxRole, this.roleValue(directShare.role));\n    }\n    \n    // Check inherited permission from folder chain\n    if (doc.folderId) {\n      const folderPerm = this.getEffectiveFolderPermission(doc.folderId, userId);\n      if (folderPerm) {\n        maxRole = Math.max(maxRole, this.roleValue(folderPerm));\n      }\n    }\n    \n    return this.roleFromValue(maxRole);\n  }\n\n  // Activity log\n  addActivity(actionType: string, userId: string, username: string, targetType: string, targetId: string, targetName: string, details?: Record<string, unknown>): ActivityEntry {\n    const entry: ActivityEntry = {\n      id: randomUUID(),\n      actionType,\n      userId,\n      username,\n      targetType,\n      targetId,\n      targetName,\n      details,\n      timestamp: new Date(),\n    };\n    this.activities.push(entry);\n    return entry;\n  }\n\n  getActivity(): ActivityEntry[] {\n    return [...this.activities].reverse(); // most recent first\n  }\n}\n\nexport const store = new Store();\n```\n\nThis is getting long but let me continue.\n\nFor auth middleware, I need to extract the token from the Authorization header and find the user.\n\n```typescript\nimport { Request, Response, NextFunction } from 'express';\nimport { createHash } from 'crypto';\nimport { store } from './store.js';\nimport { User } from './types.js';\n\nexport function hashPassword(password: string): string {\n  return createHash('sha256').update(password).digest('hex');\n}\n\nexport interface AuthRequest extends Request {\n  user?: User;\n}\n\nexport function requireAuth(req: AuthRequest, res: Response, next: NextFunction): void {\n  const authHeader = req.headers.authorization;\n  if (!authHeader || !authHeader.startsWith('Bearer ')) {\n    res.status(401).json({ error: 'Authentication required' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const token = authHeader.slice(7);\n  const userId = store.getUserIdByToken(token);\n  if (!userId) {\n    res.status(401).json({ error: 'Invalid or expired token' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const user = store.getUserById(userId);\n  if (!user) {\n    res.status(401).json({ error: 'User not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  req.user = user;\n  next();\n}\n```\n\nNow for the routes. Let me write the auth routes:\n\n```typescript\nimport { Router } from 'express';\nimport { store } from '../store.js';\nimport { hashPassword, AuthRequest } from '../auth.js';\n\nconst router = Router();\n\n// POST /api/auth/register\nrouter.post('/register', (req, res) => {\n  const { username, password } = req.body;\n  \n  if (!username || !password) {\n    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Username and password are required' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  if (typeof username !== 'string' || typeof password !== 'string') {\n    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Username and password must be strings' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  if (store.getUserByUsername(username)) {\n    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Username already exists' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const user = store.createUser(username, hashPassword(password));\n  const token = store.createToken(user.id);\n  \n  res.status(201).json({ user: { id: user.id, username: user.username }, token });\n});\n\n// POST /api/auth/login\nrouter.post('/login', (req, res) => {\n  const { username, password } = req.body;\n  \n  if (!username || !password) {\n    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Username and password are required' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const user = store.getUserByUsername(username);\n  if (!user || user.passwordHash !== hashPassword(password)) {\n    res.status(401).json({ error: 'Invalid username or password' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const token = store.createToken(user.id);\n  \n  res.json({ user: { id: user.id, username: user.username }, token });\n});\n\nexport default router;\n```\n\nFolder routes:\n\n```typescript\nimport { Router } from 'express';\nimport { store } from '../store.js';\nimport { requireAuth, AuthRequest } from '../auth.js';\n\nconst router = Router();\n\n// All folder routes require auth\nrouter.use(requireAuth);\n\n// POST /api/folders\nrouter.post('/', (req: AuthRequest, res) => {\n  const { name, parentId } = req.body;\n  \n  if (!name || typeof name !== 'string') {\n    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Name is required and must be a string' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  // If parentId is specified, check that the folder exists and user has editor access\n  if (parentId) {\n    const parentFolder = store.getFolder(parentId);\n    if (!parentFolder) {\n      res.status(404).json({ error: 'Parent folder not found' });\n      return;\n    }\n    \n    const perm = store.getEffectiveFolderPermission(parentId, req.user!.id);\n    if (!perm || perm === 'viewer') {\n      res.status(403).json({ error: 'Insufficient permissions to create folder here' });\n      return;\n    }\n  }\n  \n  const folder = store.createFolder(name, parentId || null, req.user!.id);\n  \n  store.addActivity(\n    'folder:create',\n    req.user!.id,\n    req.user!.username,\n    'folder',\n    folder.id,\n    folder.name,\n    { parentId: folder.parentId }\n  );\n  \n  res.status(201).json(folder);\n});\n\n// GET /api/folders/:id\nrouter.get('/:id', (req: AuthRequest, res) => {\n  const folder = store.getFolder(req.params.id);\n  if (!folder) {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Folder not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const perm = store.getEffectiveFolderPermission(folder.id, req.user!.id);\n  if (!perm) {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Folder not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  res.json({ ...folder, permission: perm });\n});\n\n// PUT /api/folders/:id\nrouter.put('/:id', (req: AuthRequest, res) => {\n  const { name } = req.body;\n  \n  if (!name || typeof name !== 'string') {\n    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Name is required and must be a string' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const folder = store.getFolder(req.params.id);\n  if (!folder) {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Folder not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const perm = store.getEffectiveFolderPermission(folder.id, req.user!.id);\n  if (!perm || perm === 'viewer') {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Folder not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const updated = store.updateFolder(folder.id, name);\n  \n  store.addActivity(\n    'folder:update',\n    req.user!.id,\n    req.user!.username,\n    'folder',\n    folder.id,\n    folder.name,\n    { oldName: folder.name, newName: name }\n  );\n  \n  res.json(updated);\n});\n\n// DELETE /api/folders/:id\nrouter.delete('/:id', (req: AuthRequest, res) => {\n  const folder = store.getFolder(req.params.id);\n  if (!folder) {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Folder not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const perm = store.getEffectiveFolderPermission(folder.id, req.user!.id);\n  if (perm !== 'owner') {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Folder not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const folderName = folder.name;\n  store.deleteFolder(folder.id);\n  \n  store.addActivity(\n    'folder:delete',\n    req.user!.id,\n    req.user!.username,\n    'folder',\n    req.params.id,\n    folderName\n  );\n  \n  res.status(204).send();\n});\n\n// GET /api/folders/:id/documents\nrouter.get('/:id/documents', (req: AuthRequest, res) => {\n  const folder = store.getFolder(req.params.id);\n  if (!folder) {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Folder not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const perm = store.getEffectiveFolderPermission(folder.id, req.user!.id);\n  if (!perm) {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Folder not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const docs = store.getDocumentsInFolder(folder.id);\n  res.json(docs);\n});\n\n// GET /api/folders/:id/folders\nrouter.get('/:id/folders', (req: AuthRequest, res) => {\n  const folder = store.getFolder(req.params.id);\n  if (!folder) {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Folder not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const perm = store.getEffectiveFolderPermission(folder.id, req.user!.id);\n  if (!perm) {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Folder not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const folders = store.getChildFolders(folder.id);\n  res.json(folders);\n});\n\nexport default router;\n```\n\nDocument routes:\n\n```typescript\nimport { Router } from 'express';\nimport { store } from '../store.js';\nimport { requireAuth, AuthRequest } from '../auth.js';\n\nconst router = Router();\n\nrouter.use(requireAuth);\n\n// POST /api/documents\nrouter.post('/', (req: AuthRequest, res) => {\n  const { title, content, folderId } = req.body;\n  \n  if (!title || typeof title !== 'string') {\n    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Title is required and must be a string' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  if (typeof content !== 'string') {\n    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Content must be a string' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  if (!folderId) {\n    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Folder ID is required' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const folder = store.getFolder(folderId);\n  if (!folder) {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Folder not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  // Need at least editor on the parent folder to create documents\n  const perm = store.getEffectiveFolderPermission(folderId, req.user!.id);\n  if (!perm || perm === 'viewer') {\n    res.status(403).json({ error: 'Insufficient permissions to create document in this folder' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const doc = store.createDocument(title, content || '', folderId, req.user!.id);\n  \n  store.addActivity(\n    'document:create',\n    req.user!.id,\n    req.user!.username,\n    'document',\n    doc.id,\n    doc.title,\n    { folderId }\n  );\n  \n  res.status(201).json(doc);\n});\n\n// GET /api/documents/:id\nrouter.get('/:id', (req: AuthRequest, res) => {\n  const doc = store.getDocument(req.params.id);\n  if (!doc) {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Document not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const perm = store.getEffectiveDocumentPermission(doc.id, req.user!.id);\n  if (!perm) {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Document not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  res.json({ ...doc, permission: perm });\n});\n\n// PUT /api/documents/:id\nrouter.put('/:id', (req: AuthRequest, res) => {\n  const { title, content } = req.body;\n  \n  if (!title || typeof title !== 'string') {\n    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Title is required and must be a string' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  if (typeof content !== 'string') {\n    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Content must be a string' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const doc = store.getDocument(req.params.id);\n  if (!doc) {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Document not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const perm = store.getEffectiveDocumentPermission(doc.id, req.user!.id);\n  if (!perm || perm === 'viewer') {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Document not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const updated = store.updateDocument(doc.id, title, content);\n  \n  store.addActivity(\n    'document:update',\n    req.user!.id,\n    req.user!.username,\n    'document',\n    doc.id,\n    doc.title,\n    { oldTitle: doc.title, newTitle: title }\n  );\n  \n  res.json(updated);\n});\n\n// DELETE /api/documents/:id\nrouter.delete('/:id', (req: AuthRequest, res) => {\n  const doc = store.getDocument(req.params.id);\n  if (!doc) {\n    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Document not found' });\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  const perm = store.getEffectiveDocumentPermission(doc.id, req.user!.id);\n  if